WEBVTT

00:00:00.300 --> 00:00:04.381
Every BxAgents project can ship its own chat page.

00:00:04.831 --> 00:00:09.540
This is the web UI of an Acme support agent, built from one gateway file.

00:00:09.990 --> 00:00:13.362
It starts at sign in, with accounts you declare in code.

00:00:15.363 --> 00:00:17.438
Signed in, you land in a clean chat.

00:00:17.888 --> 00:00:22.588
The header shows the agent and its controls: your conversations, the model

00:00:22.588 --> 00:00:25.192
picker, notes, an API key, and the theme.

00:00:27.191 --> 00:00:31.486
Ask a question and the answer streams in as it is written, with Markdown

00:00:31.486 --> 00:00:32.738
formatting and lists.

00:00:35.701 --> 00:00:38.914
The model picker lists the profiles the app chose to offer.

00:00:39.364 --> 00:00:43.901
Pick the planner profile, and the next answer comes from a different model, in

00:00:43.901 --> 00:00:45.180
the same conversation.

00:00:47.180 --> 00:00:51.889
When the agent calls a tool, the page shows it as a block you can open, with the

00:00:51.889 --> 00:00:54.244
tool's name and what it was called with.

00:00:56.243 --> 00:00:57.959
Every conversation is saved.

00:00:58.409 --> 00:01:03.208
Start a new chat, and the old one stays in the list, ready to open again.

00:01:05.208 --> 00:01:07.982
Notes keep what the agent should remember about you.

00:01:08.432 --> 00:01:10.976
Add one, and it is there next time.

00:01:12.975 --> 00:01:16.527
Dark mode is one click, and the page remembers your choice.

00:01:18.527 --> 00:01:23.196
That is the whole web UI: sign in, streaming answers, a model picker you

00:01:23.196 --> 00:01:26.698
control, tools, saved conversations, notes and themes.

00:01:27.148 --> 00:01:30.122
All from a few lines of YAML and one gateway file.

